# pico_cam_a

RP2040 with 16 MB W25Q128 flash, a 240 by 135 ST7789 LCD, and an HM01B0
grayscale camera. The SDK bridge selects waveshare_pico_cam_a, retaining the
pico Arm lane while using the correct flash capacity and UART0 on GP0/GP1.
There is no user LED. The exposed default I2C is I2C1 on GP2/GP3.

LCD: SPI1 clock GP10, MOSI GP11, CS GP13, DC GP9, reset GP7. The
backlight is permanently powered; GP14 is the camera pixel clock.
Camera: I2C0 SDA GP4/SCL GP5, address 0x24; serial data GP6, PCLK GP14,
LVLD GP15, FVLD GP16. A dedicated 36 MHz oscillator supplies MCLK; there
is no GPIO reset or XCLK. K3 and K4 are active-low buttons on GP18/GP19.
The ADC reference is the filtered 3V3 rail. GP24 reads the USB VBUS divider.

The schematic is authoritative where the demo differs: its LCD_BL=14,
camera reset=2 and XCLK=3 must not be driven. The vendor demo also allocates
324 by 324 bytes despite naming its initialization table 324x244. The
provider matches that square output (register 0x3010=0), captures the full
frame, and leaves cropping or resizing to the preview module.

Capture owns I2C0 and GP4/5/6/14/15/16 until sleep. Use from one core;
initialization and capture are synchronous. PIO and DMA resources are claimed
dynamically and released by sleep. No hardware qualification has been done.

Sources:
https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/PICO-Cam-A
https://files.waveshare.com/wiki/PICO-Cam-A/PICO-Cam-A.pdf
https://files.waveshare.com/wiki/PICO-Cam-A/PICO-Cam-A.zip
